Subject: [PATCH] FindStoneFor: drop the sharpening stone from the weightstone list

WHY THIS PATCH EXISTS
    `uPrioritizedWeightStoneIds` - the list consulted for MACE, MACE2, STAFF
    and FIST weapons - contains ELEMENTAL_SHARPENING_STONE. That is a
    copy-paste from the sharpening-stone list three lines above. A sharpening
    stone is a bladed-weapon enchant; handing one to a mace produces exactly
    the same SPELL_FAILED_EQUIPPED_ITEM_CLASS rejection that 0001 fixes, only
    at level 60+, since item 18262 is level 60 content.

    There is no correct value to put in its place: mod-playerbots' own
    `enum WeightstoneId` (src/Bot/PlayerbotAI.h:200-208) has no elemental
    tier, because no Elemental Weightstone item exists - the weightstone
    progression goes Dense (12643) straight to Fel (28420). So the entry is
    deleted rather than corrected.

    This is a pure removal from a static initialiser list. It cannot change
    the shape of any type or signature, so it carries no compile risk beyond
    the patch itself applying.

WHAT WOULD LET THIS PATCH BE DELETED
    mod-playerbots removing ELEMENTAL_SHARPENING_STONE from
    `uPrioritizedWeightStoneIds`. When that lands and AC_MODULE_SHA is bumped
    past it, this patch stops applying and fails the build on purpose - at
    which point delete this file.

    Upstream PR: not yet opened. Add the link here when it is.

APPLIES TO
    mod-playerbots @ 8d9f6aa6bc6d45f9ae0ee0675b9b1f8aa6937312, on top of 0001
    src/Bot/PlayerbotAI.cpp:5567-5569 (uPrioritizedWeightStoneIds)

--- a/src/Bot/PlayerbotAI.cpp
+++ b/src/Bot/PlayerbotAI.cpp
@@ -5574,7 +5574,7 @@
         SOLID_SHARPENING_STONE,      HEAVY_SHARPENING_STONE, COARSE_SHARPENING_STONE,    ROUGH_SHARPENING_STONE};
 
     static const std::vector<uint32_t> uPrioritizedWeightStoneIds = {
-        ADAMANTITE_WEIGHTSTONE, FEL_WEIGHTSTONE,    ELEMENTAL_SHARPENING_STONE, DENSE_WEIGHTSTONE, SOLID_WEIGHTSTONE,
+        ADAMANTITE_WEIGHTSTONE, FEL_WEIGHTSTONE,    DENSE_WEIGHTSTONE, SOLID_WEIGHTSTONE,
         HEAVY_WEIGHTSTONE,      COARSE_WEIGHTSTONE, ROUGH_WEIGHTSTONE};
 
     Item* stone = nullptr;
